hip-reqd-work-group-size: a fix to intel/llvm v7.1.1, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

The AMDGPU backend sizes a kernel's register budget by the "amdgpu-flat-work-group-size" attribute, which clang sets
from reqd_work_group_size for OpenCL kernels and from --gpu-max-threads-per-block for HIP ones, but not for SYCL
kernels: a SYCL kernel's [[sycl::reqd_work_group_size(N)]] or work_group_size property went only into the reqd_work_group_size metadata, which
the backend does not read for this, so every SYCL kernel was budgeted for 1024 work-items (on gfx1150: 128 VGPRs;
the int8 expert product's 64 x 128 tile spilled 12-26 registers, with the attribute 135 and none).  The attribute
is now set from the SYCL kernel's reqd_work_group_size as it is from OpenCL's.
In v7.2.0 clang already sets it for SYCL kernels (AMDGPU.cpp); this keeps the part for the lowered attributes (CompileTimePropertiesPass).
---
diff --git a/llvm/lib/SYCLLowerIR/CompileTimePropertiesPass.cpp b/llvm/lib/SYCLLowerIR/CompileTimePropertiesPass.cpp
index 313bbdc46f..357dc45235 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/SYCLLowerIR/CompileTimePropertiesPass.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/SYCLLowerIR/CompileTimePropertiesPass.cpp
@@ -394,6 +394,20 @@ attributeToExecModeMetadata(const Attribute &Attr, Function &F) {
       MDVals.push_back(ConstantAsMetadata::get(
           Constant::getIntegerValue(SizeTTy, APInt(SizeTBitSize, 1, 10))));
 
+    // The AMDGPU backend budgets a kernel's registers by this attribute
+    // (1024 work-items without it), not by the metadata: a required or
+    // largest work-group size bounds it, as clang does for OpenCL's.
+    if (Triple(F.getParent()->getTargetTriple()).isAMDGCN() &&
+        (AttrKindStr == "sycl-work-group-size" ||
+         AttrKindStr == "sycl-max-work-group-size")) {
+      uint64_t Lanes = 1;
+      for (Metadata *MDVal : MDVals)
+        Lanes *= cast<ConstantAsMetadata>(MDVal)->getValue()->getUniqueInteger().getZExtValue();
+      F.addFnAttr("amdgpu-flat-work-group-size",
+                  (AttrKindStr == "sycl-work-group-size" ? std::to_string(Lanes) : std::string("1")) +
+                      "," + std::to_string(Lanes));
+    }
+
     if (NumDims < 3) {
       if (!F.hasMetadata("work_group_num_dim"))
         F.setMetadata("work_group_num_dim",
